## **PHASE 6: Kafka Consumer & Analytics Processing**

### 6.1 Create Video Analytics Service
- [ ] Create `src/main/java/com/videoanalytics/service/VideoAnalyticsService.java`:
  ```java
  @Service
  @Slf4j
  public class VideoAnalyticsService {
    @Autowired
    private VideoAnalyticsRepository analyticsRepo;

    @Transactional
    public void processEvent(VideoEventDTO event) {
      VideoAnalytics analytics = analyticsRepo.findById(event.getVideoId())
        .orElseGet(() -> {
          VideoAnalytics newAnalytics = new VideoAnalytics();
          newAnalytics.setVideoId(event.getVideoId());
          return newAnalytics;
        });

      switch (event.getEventType()) {
        case PLAY:
          analytics.setPlayCount(analytics.getPlayCount() + 1);
          analytics.setTotalViews(analytics.getTotalViews() + 1);
          break;
        case PAUSE:
          analytics.setPauseCount(analytics.getPauseCount() + 1);
          break;
        case SEEK:
          analytics.setSeekCount(analytics.getSeekCount() + 1);
          break;
        case BUFFER_START:
        case BUFFER_END:
        case QUALITY_CHANGE:
          // No increment for these
          break;
        case ENDED:
          Long watchedSeconds = event.getWatchedSeconds() != null ? event.getWatchedSeconds() : 0;
          analytics.setTotalPlaytimeSeconds(analytics.getTotalPlaytimeSeconds() + watchedSeconds);
          break;
      }

      analyticsRepo.save(analytics);
      log.debug("Updated analytics for video: {}", event.getVideoId());
    }
  }
  ```

